{"title":"Kinetic Connections: Movement for Healthy Aging - Free Trial (40+)","startsAt":"2026-10-21T13:30:00-04:00","endsAt":"2026-10-21T15:30:00-04:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"🎟️ **Registration is required in advance.**\n**Please note:** RSVP’ing on Meetup does **not** reserve your spot.\n[Register online](https://app.amilia.com/store/en/miles-nadal-jcc/api/Activity/Detail?activityId=yP0NoWr) or call **416-924-6211 ext. 0**\n\nJoin us for **Kinetic Connections: Movement for Healthy Aging**, a welcoming movement and dance program for adults 40+ of all abilities.\nLooking for a supportive way to stay active, move with greater ease, and connect with others? **Kinetic Connections** offers a gentle and engaging approach to movement through music, breath awareness, imagination, and creative exploration.\n\nLed by instructor **Julia Sasso**, each class encourages you to move at your own pace and discover ways of moving that feel comfortable, enjoyable, and natural to you. Regular participation can help support balance, coordination, strength, flexibility, mobility, and overall well-being, while creating opportunities for creativity, self-expression, and social connection.\n\nNo previous dance experience is required. Whether you're returning to movement, looking for a new way to stay active, or simply want to enjoy moving in a welcoming environment, everyone is encouraged to participate in a way that feels right for them.\nCome curious, comfortable, and ready to move!\n\n## Event Details\n\n📍 **Location:** Miles Nadal JCC – 750 Spadina Ave. (enter through the Spadina doors)\n💃 **Format:** Guided movement and dance class\n👥 **Age:** 40+\n📅 **Session:** 6-week program\n⏱️ **Class length:** 60 minutes\n\n## What to Expect\n\n✔️ Gentle, accessible movement suitable for all abilities\n✔️ Guided exploration through music, breath, and imagination\n✔️ Movement at your own pace and comfort level\n✔️ Exercises that support balance, coordination, strength, flexibility, and mobility\n✔️ Opportunities for creativity and self-expression\n✔️ A welcoming environment that encourages connection and community\n✔️ No previous dance experience required\n\n## About the Instructor\n\n**Julia Sasso** has enjoyed a distinguished career as a performer, choreographer, and dance educator spanning several decades. Throughout her work, she has been passionate about helping people discover the benefits and joy of movement at every stage of life.\nJulia’s classes create a supportive space to explore movement, build confidence, and connect with others while encouraging curiosity, creativity, and overall well-being.\n\nWhether you’re looking to stay active, improve your mobility, reduce stress, try something new, or simply enjoy an hour of movement and connection each week, **Kinetic Connections** is a welcoming place to move, explore, and feel good.\nCome experience the joy of moving well! ✨","venue":{"name":"Miles Nadal","address":"750 Spadina Ave, Room 317b, M5S 2J2, Toronto","lat":43.66621,"lng":-79.40402,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":null,"group":"Downtown Toronto Martial Arts & Dance","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/a/c/1/2/highres_532904050.jpeg"}